[{:db/id "q-74420/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" :answer/id #uuid "a00af17c-fb49-5798-9579-c60050f6a391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "72c9aa6f-038d-5947-a747-fee648d6d2b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" :answer/id #uuid "486f8e76-0a35-5911-a176-8ad71b901e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420/selection/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe" :answer/id #uuid "9dcf41b7-958b-5f40-a621-bc9736375cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "ba47b6f4-1116-5380-8e28-847dd10c0cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a0aa31-08e7-5a59-80ba-f19b542d795b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74420/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" :answer-field/choices ["q-74420/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" "q-74420/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-74420/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" "q-74420/selection/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe" "q-74420/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74420" :question/id #uuid "5b774691-7eb0-591e-a16e-3aca9ee0bcfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74420" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(5,-8)$ and the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's draw a diagram describing our situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008611/assets/6ec04fe0ad996f87dbc07b0883afb3fa7aef1429412a550afe9102d1c22db71b.png)\n\n  \n\nFirst, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=\\frac{1}{3}x-3$ and passes through the point $(5,-8).$\n\n The given line has a slope of $\\frac{1}{3},$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-3.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+8 & =-3(x-5) \\\\ y+8 & =-3x+15 \\\\ y & =-3x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{1}{3}x-3 \\\\ y=-3x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x-3 & =-3x+7 \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{3}x & =7+3 \\\\ \\frac{10}{3}x & =10 \\\\ x & =10\\cdot \\frac{3}{10} \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-2.$ So, our solution is $x=3$ and $y=-2.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(3,-2).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(5,-8)$ and $(3,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-5)^{2}+(-2-(-8))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(5,-8)$ and the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x-3$ is $2\\sqrt{10}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74420/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7030a12-bd18-5f8b-84eb-28b6f216f972"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74420"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection/d00a32d7a1eb9c96825aa2e78d664ca524d564836a7f92d25cb0da94278c3bbf" :answer/id #uuid "2a09cf91-4618-5c5e-957b-da3f37105e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection/70596445916736200d9cccde384a7f075288252ca8802b2d258ec1d29ae3eeae" :answer/id #uuid "32d6fcac-72f7-5ecd-a223-3b06c843a4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{29}{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection/993c61658b69129b7a7efd4fa0360a394f7a9ad2859379dce4753b811c3c4247" :answer/id #uuid "a56dd61d-5e4e-50ba-bfee-74ae1ebb7a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-\\frac{13}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection/bbfce6d94710509efea28d70ea65ff06bf4f462cfc0e3475f688bb95aaf7883b" :answer/id #uuid "d8b178ed-3889-5cd7-b417-46b855678559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection/5ce995436c8df2cfa109533154d61dbec15b632c622750ccbcabe8b074ab4b73" :answer/id #uuid "a33dfab3-81bf-5fee-94e3-3c7633339521" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},-\\frac{15}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5161e89e-3259-5133-baec-108e1f3b561a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74421/selection/bbfce6d94710509efea28d70ea65ff06bf4f462cfc0e3475f688bb95aaf7883b" :answer-field/choices ["q-74421/selection/d00a32d7a1eb9c96825aa2e78d664ca524d564836a7f92d25cb0da94278c3bbf" "q-74421/selection/70596445916736200d9cccde384a7f075288252ca8802b2d258ec1d29ae3eeae" "q-74421/selection/993c61658b69129b7a7efd4fa0360a394f7a9ad2859379dce4753b811c3c4247" "q-74421/selection/bbfce6d94710509efea28d70ea65ff06bf4f462cfc0e3475f688bb95aaf7883b" "q-74421/selection/5ce995436c8df2cfa109533154d61dbec15b632c622750ccbcabe8b074ab4b73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74421" :question/id #uuid "0b8e0f60-8eba-5366-a303-55d3880df894" :question/math-academy-id "q-74421" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008611/assets/67d09cf1ebb51a37c122ea1e0bb53b0bcabedca0251ae4105ebb93dd55d111dd.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-8$ that is closest to the point $(-4,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-8$ and passes through the point $(-4,-1).$\n\n The given line has a slope of $\\frac{3}{2},$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =-\\frac{2}{3}(x+4) \\\\ y+1 & =-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=\\frac{3}{2}x-8 \\\\ y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}x-8 & =-\\frac{2}{3}x-\\frac{11}{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x+\\frac{2}{3}x & =8-\\frac{11}{3} \\\\ \\frac{13}{6}x & =\\frac{13}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{13}{3}\\cdot \\frac{6}{13} \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-5.$ So, our solution is $x=2$ and $y=-5.$ Therefore, the lines intersect at the point $(2,-5).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the point on the line $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-8$ that is closest to the point $(-4,-1)$ is $(2,-5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "5eee4826-c0d8-57b2-b805-ffee4f0f49ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" :answer/id #uuid "a8c5aaa8-564a-5055-abda-0505abccc889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" :answer/id #uuid "0b6aac72-9505-53be-98fa-6e7d29c83b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "33f2da1d-9fad-5d80-a6c6-f54397460284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037" :answer/id #uuid "a74a12c4-ad75-5cc5-a635-64422a008747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dddba98-7e9e-5b36-bb9f-eda5f9aa09c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74435/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer-field/choices ["q-74435/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" "q-74435/selection/e59e169232e16e8d4fc95e4d14f7ebab8f0ea66430d2fabd4381548437f83344" "q-74435/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" "q-74435/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-74435/selection/faad0727b2c62b6cced88abf9b210ea8763c2fd1c03c01c27346d66484992037"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74435" :question/id #uuid "6c55d79c-0527-5806-9fec-32477e380606" :question/math-academy-id "q-74435" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $(-3,-6)$ and the line $y+2x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the equation of the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2x & =-2 \\\\ y & =-2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's draw a diagram describing our situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008611/assets/789659bd700bc5f8407d409bc28bf5ce5309369af2aa5ad5973434d47cff74fa.png)\n\n \n\nNext, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=-2x-2$ and passes through the point $(-3,-6).$\n\n The given line has a slope of $-2,$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+3) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=-2x-2 \\\\ y=\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -2x-\\frac{1}{2}x & =2-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}x & =-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ into either of the two equations gives $y=-4.$ So, our solution is $x=1$ and $y=-4.$ So, the lines intersect at the point $(1,-4).$\n\nFinally, we find the distance $d$ between the points $(-3,-6)$ and $(1,-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-3))}^{2}+(-4-(-6))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the shortest distance between the point $(-3,-6)$ and the line $y+2x=-2$ is $2\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74435/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7030a12-bd18-5f8b-84eb-28b6f216f972"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74435"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection/20239ce13ebeb8ea9a6e3fe4bc1df2bcd198773fee0af9e8c748c157f519c915" :answer/id #uuid "cc6a53a4-8e37-5e81-924b-1e385cd14ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{7}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection/3b7e6455199238f5ff8ee4b817acba8105dc7a0293452495acd7398277447c44" :answer/id #uuid "8cf8c5b2-b1d6-50a3-97ac-f53d4d6eb0d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{5},\\frac{1}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection/7f7a05ec9be07061809d04d3d7c14f23856521ebc8af4ebe2069d736c23b0ce7" :answer/id #uuid "df7b9cc4-6d1c-57cf-95cf-8f455ed20d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection/85029f8f3872971f826711e5bf140761741ea6acc3dad7a5b81578adb466aa6f" :answer/id #uuid "0237db8d-e99e-59b3-83af-bc307b74484c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{7}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection/3f3233172416ee1aa4c5a4da4f346942c4148192746a656a2a5bc3b9f3348976" :answer/id #uuid "721915e8-1e4e-51ef-915f-efa3f36d7eb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{5},-\\frac{7}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae89664c-33dc-5fe9-b389-27232ac8691f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114346/selection/85029f8f3872971f826711e5bf140761741ea6acc3dad7a5b81578adb466aa6f" :answer-field/choices ["q-114346/selection/20239ce13ebeb8ea9a6e3fe4bc1df2bcd198773fee0af9e8c748c157f519c915" "q-114346/selection/3b7e6455199238f5ff8ee4b817acba8105dc7a0293452495acd7398277447c44" "q-114346/selection/7f7a05ec9be07061809d04d3d7c14f23856521ebc8af4ebe2069d736c23b0ce7" "q-114346/selection/85029f8f3872971f826711e5bf140761741ea6acc3dad7a5b81578adb466aa6f" "q-114346/selection/3f3233172416ee1aa4c5a4da4f346942c4148192746a656a2a5bc3b9f3348976"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114346" :question/id #uuid "56d55b4f-72ce-5ee5-9de8-d9307974b602" :question/math-academy-id "q-114346" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008611/assets/df3838ae44d1477a4a0de303972cd26a2ceaad9b213f1d8e4be3a53bd453aeb2.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $y-3x=2$ that is closest to the point $(4,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the equation of the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3x & =2 \\\\ y & =3x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=3x+2$ and passes through the point $(4,0).$\n\nThe given line has a slope of $3,$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x-4) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=3x+2 \\\\ y=-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2 & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 3x+\\frac{1}{3}x & =\\frac{4}{3}-2 \\\\ \\frac{10}{3}x & =-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 10x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{1}{5}$ into either of the two equations gives $y=\\frac{7}{5}.$ So, our solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{5}$ and $y=\\frac{7}{5}.$ So, the lines intersect at the point $(-\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{7}{5}).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the point on the line  $y-3x=2$ that is closest to the point $(4,0)$ is  $(-\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{7}{5}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114346/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114346"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection/db1d4aae48c6b0ee39822fa5e21ea246e827482cc7d601d1a986a9f540def415" :answer/id #uuid "ee95ac48-a793-5be2-88b8-aa349fc88509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{9}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection/825e624fd62bdd1d4985f6de568baa2ebce6af40bc16c6c9faf2e4ae5e55425b" :answer/id #uuid "fbd880a2-7d10-54b3-a20e-36c8ce0c6562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{9}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection/b8a3c1dbef37575deef86cb11378d8367b26b4c141213c9ca252de1568226d9c" :answer/id #uuid "1c925840-af98-5293-a158-18de64b924cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{5},-\\frac{9}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection/ec5d6e0d64e0ac3e4fb7a02195c646cf5ec0562602730fdc32c4ae08188bbf69" :answer/id #uuid "388cb135-019f-5948-858a-1b6fa823e314" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{9}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection/c2df16b6d8b0765f1ae9a13a3d2cbd107dee1802bafe228be2835e272f171a8c" :answer/id #uuid "77096218-1510-53aa-ba99-2cece25e273a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{5},\\frac{2}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee119671-d7ba-5016-9310-e15749d4d416" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114349/selection/ec5d6e0d64e0ac3e4fb7a02195c646cf5ec0562602730fdc32c4ae08188bbf69" :answer-field/choices ["q-114349/selection/db1d4aae48c6b0ee39822fa5e21ea246e827482cc7d601d1a986a9f540def415" "q-114349/selection/825e624fd62bdd1d4985f6de568baa2ebce6af40bc16c6c9faf2e4ae5e55425b" "q-114349/selection/b8a3c1dbef37575deef86cb11378d8367b26b4c141213c9ca252de1568226d9c" "q-114349/selection/ec5d6e0d64e0ac3e4fb7a02195c646cf5ec0562602730fdc32c4ae08188bbf69" "q-114349/selection/c2df16b6d8b0765f1ae9a13a3d2cbd107dee1802bafe228be2835e272f171a8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114349" :question/id #uuid "d186a0b8-cfb0-554c-a5c7-b433b90e0491" :question/math-academy-id "q-114349" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008611/assets/ba46b4f3f458a6be13ea01ca1351658c102732db94e22725890afaaade6fc904.png)\n\nFind the point on the line $5y-10x=5$ that is closest to the point $(-2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the equation of the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-10x & =5 \\\\ 5y & =10x+5 \\\\ y & =2x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the equation of the line that's perpendicular to $y=2x+1$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe given line has a slope of $2,$ so our perpendicular line must have a slope of $-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing point-slope form and simplifying, we obtain the equation of the perpendicular line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-1+3 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now find the point where the two lines intersect. To do this, we solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=2x+1 \\\\ y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this system by putting the two equations equal to one another and solving for $x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{1}{2}x & =2-1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}x & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{2}{5}$ into either of the two equations gives $y=\\frac{9}{5}.$ So, our solution is $x=\\frac{2}{5}$ and $y=\\frac{9}{5}.$ So, the lines intersect at the point $(\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{9}{5}).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the point on the line  $5y-10x=5$ that is closest to the point $(-2,3)$ is  $(\\frac{2}{5},\\frac{9}{5}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114349/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "59d3a391-c163-5a04-944c-5d61a3950e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114349"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
